linux (6.12.85-1+untangle4trixie) current; urgency=medium

  * NGFW-16021: port physdev patch from 5.10 to 6.12
  * Adds FDB lookup to xt_physdev match so physdev-out is populated
    for IP-forwarded bridge traffic. Required for per-port dst-intf
    marking in bridge mode with ebtables broute.
  * br_nf_core.c: br_nf_get_outdev() helper performs RCU-safe FDB
    lookup via br_fdb_find_rcu() + neighbor/ARP resolution. Device
    pointer extracted inside RCU critical section.
  * xt_physdev.c: calls br_nf_get_outdev() before match_outdev when
    physoutdev is not yet set.
  * Restores Bullseye-equivalent physdev-out behavior for physical
    egress port reporting and hairpin NAT connmark accuracy.

 -- Rohit Singh <rohit@arista.com>  Fri, 03 Oct 2026 10:00:00 +0530

linux (6.12.85-1+untangle3trixie) current; urgency=medium

  * NGFW-15749: disable enable_signed in amd64/defines.toml.
  * Trixie's gencontrol.py splits image+meta+udeb packages into
    a separate linux-signed-amd64 source bundle when enable_signed
    is true. We don't build that pipeline (NGFW kernels are not
    Secure-Boot signed -- confirmed via sbverify on bookworm).
  * Setting enable_signed=false routes all packages back to the
    unsigned source bundle, restoring bookworm-equivalent behavior:
    bare-named linux-image-untangle-amd64, image meta, headers
    meta, AND ~45 installer udebs all emitted from one build.
  * Replaces the previous gencontrol.py udeb patch from untangle2,
    which is now redundant and would cause duplicate package
    registration if kept.
  * signed-template package is no longer emitted (unused; nothing
    downstream consumes it).

 -- Rohit Singh <rohit@arista.com>  Wed, 06 May 2026 14:00:00 +0530

linux (6.12.85-1+untangle2trixie) current; urgency=medium

  * NGFW-15749: emit installer udebs from unsigned source build
  * Trixie split installer udebs into separate linux-signed-amd64
    source pkg; we don't build that pipeline. Patch gencontrol.py
    to register real udeb packages against the unsigned bundle so
    kernel-wedge runs and ~50 *-di_*.udeb get built.
  * Required for bootable Trixie d-i ISO with matching kernel ABI.

